course: dictionary
lesson: 5023
title: Light our eyes cannot see
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some light is invisible to our eyes. Infrared is one kind, and it sits just beyond red light on the colour scale. We cannot see it, but we can feel it as heat. «Infrared and heat cameras film at night by catching light or warmth our eyes cannot see.»
explain: Context helps you work out what infrared means. In «Automatic doors use sensors, some with a radar beam and some with infrared light, to detect people coming», the word sensors tells you the light is used to notice things, not to light up a room.
explain: Infrared is part of a bigger family. «Light we can see is only a small part of a wider range that includes radio waves, microwaves, infrared, ultraviolet, X-rays and gamma rays.» So visible light is just a small slice of all the light there is.
explain: Look for phrases too. «Infrared light», «infrared camera» and «infrared sensor» all name things that use this hidden light. Read the words around the word to see what the thing does.
fact: Infrared is a kind of light that our eyes cannot see.
fact: Infrared sits just beyond red light, and we feel it as heat.
fact: «Infrared» can describe things, as in «infrared camera», or name the light itself.
fact: Infrared is used in TV remote controls, motion sensors and thermal cameras.
fact: «Light we can see is only a small part of a wider range» that includes infrared, ultraviolet and X-rays.
exercise: «Automatic doors use sensors, some with infrared light, to detect people coming.» What do some of these sensors use to notice people? | Loud music | Sand and water | *Infrared light | Baking soda
exercise: «Warm animals glow bright on heat cameras, while cold ground looks dark.» Why does the ground look dark? | It is painted black | It is far away from the camera | *It is cold, so it gives out little heat | It is covered in leaves
exercise: Infrared light sits just beyond which colour of visible light? | *Red | Blue | Green | Violet
test: Which everyday thing uses infrared to help work its buttons from across the room? | Mirror | Microwave oven | *TV remote control | Torch
test: What do we feel when infrared light hits our skin? | *Heat | Cold | Wind | Sound
exam: Which is part of the wider range of light that includes radio waves, ultraviolet and X-rays? | *Infrared | Shadow | Sunlight | Rainbow
